# lever: L1 featurisation prefetch + WRITER output writer thread + autotune-retry fix (run_alphafold.py; flags --featurisation_workers/--featurisation_prefetch, --output_writer)
# what: (L1) featurise upcoming (input, seed) items in forked worker processes with the identical featurise_input call while the GPU runs the current item (needs --norun_data_pipeline so every work item is known up front); (fix) the fork's tokamax autotune attempt is made once per process and its failure printed once, instead of a failed 10-25 s attempt per new bucket; the jitted forward is exposed as ModelRunner._jitted_apply (the same hk.transform + jax.jit as upstream's _model, which becomes functools.partial(_jitted_apply, params)); (WRITER) with --output_writer each fold job's result extraction (extract_inference_results / embeddings / distogram) and write_outputs run on ONE writer thread, in submission order, while the next fold job's inference runs — the same calls, the same files; every pending job is written ('Fold job … done') before 'Done running N fold jobs.'
# why-faster: removes 1.4-10 s of CPU featurisation per seed from the GPU's critical path (GPU duty cycle 66% -> 84%); first-in-bucket cost no longer includes a repeated failed autotune; (WRITER) the 1.5-2 s of host-side result extraction + file writing per fold job (about 5 % of a 1,200-token fast item on H100) leave the GPU's critical path in a multi-job pass: per-item wall -2.4 % at 448 and -3.8 % at 1,216 padded tokens, the inference timer unchanged
# numerics class: bitwise vs stock that loaded the same --cache_dir (XLA autotune results)
# RNG: unchanged (each item is featurised with its own RandomState(seed) exactly as upstream; jax PRNGKey(seed) untouched)
# measured: 1.27-1.40x job wall against the stock script run before and after it on the same H100 host, 16 inputs x 5 seeds at 167-705 tokens (HOWTO.md §1)
# applies-to: github.com/sokrypton/alphafold3@bc32b22ff5902e3daffd5d1f7203d7f2ab6cb997 (upstream google-deepmind/alphafold3 main: the L1 hunks apply to the same functions; the tokamax-autotune block is fork-specific)
# default: off (both flags default to upstream behaviour; opt-in, numerics class unchanged when on)
